      "sha256_sample": "f5af5002a0385ae9438d67ae4221335829ca57db3227f714f474df6c105f7a82",
      "excerpts": [
        {
          "line": 1,
          "text": "# Sonic"
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "Building Sonic requires both a Go (version 1.27 or later) and a C compiler. You can install"
        },
        {
          "line": 13,
          "text": "The build outputs are ```build/sonicd``` and ```build/sonictool``` executables."
        },
        {
          "line": 15,
          "text": "## Initialization of the Sonic Database"
        },
        {
          "line": 17,
          "text": "You will need a genesis file to join a network. See [lachesis_launch](https://github.com/Fantom-foundation/lachesis_launch) for details on obtaining one. Once you have a genesis file, initialize the DB:"
        },
        {
          "line": 20,
          "text": "sonictool --datadir=<target DB path> genesis <path to the genesis file>"
        },
        {
          "line": 23,
          "text": "## Running `sonicd`"
        },
        {
          "line": 27,
          "text": "on how you can run your own `sonicd` instance."
        },
        {
          "line": 31,
          "text": "To launch a `sonicd` read-only (non-validator) node for network specified by the genesis file:"
        },
        {
          "line": 34,
          "text": "sonicd --datadir=<DB path>"
        },
        {
          "line": 39,
          "text": "As an alternative to passing the numerous flags to the `sonicd` binary, you can also pass a"
        },
        {
          "line": 43,
          "text": "sonicd --datadir=<DB path> --config /path/to/your/config.toml"
        },
        {
          "line": 50,
          "text": "sonictool --datadir=<DB path> dumpconfig"
        },
        {
          "line": 58,
          "text": "sonictool --datadir=<DB path> validator new"
        },
        {
          "line": 61,
          "text": "To launch a validator, use the `--validator.id` and `--validator.pubkey` flags. See the [Sonic Documentation](https://docs.soniclabs.com/) for details on obtaining a validator ID and registering your initial stake."
        },
        {
          "line": 64,
          "text": "sonicd --datadir=<DB path> --validator.id=YOUR_ID --validator.pubkey=0xYOUR_PUBKEY"
        },
        {
          "line": 67,
          "text": "`sonicd` will prompt for a password to decrypt your validator private key. Optionally, use `--validator.password` to specify a password file."
        },
        {
          "line": 74,
          "text": "sonicd --datadir=<DB path> --nat=extip:1.2.3.4"
        }
      ],
      "success": true
    },
